# Fixed defect 2379, 2026-11-10, lane b29-pkgmsg: a file of the package
# `core` calls `mine()`, which only the program's own `other/strings`
# declares, a module no `use` of a package's file can name (spec § 1).
#
# SYMPTOM: `unknown_name` with `did you mean find?`, `fix (guess): rename to
# find` and a note on binding a C function, all pointing away from the cause.
#
# CAUSE: the lookup of a name declared elsewhere answered nothing where its
# one module was out of the file's reach (defect 2373's repair), so the name
# was told as one nothing declares.
#
# FIX: the name is told with the module that declares it and why no line of
# the file reaches it, and no near name is offered.
use <core>/strings

use other/strings as own

function main()
    print(strings.word() + own.mine())
